finding: P2: Native Windows cargo selection leaves the crate's cross-build linker configuration active. src/native/index.ts now selects cargo build on win32, but crates/native/.cargo/config.toml still forces linker = "lld-link", and cargoBuild does not override it. A normal Rust MSVC + Visual Studio C++ installation without standalone LLVM therefore fails linking rather than building with its native link.exe. The existing WSL devShellBuild explicitly overrides this exact configuration to link.exe; the new native Windows path does not. windows-latest's broader installed toolchain masks this dependency, and the oracle only asserts invocation.kind. Smallest fix: override CARGO_TARGET_X86_64_PC_WINDOWS_MSVC_LINKER for native Windows MSVC builds (or scope/remove the cross-only linker config so Cargo discovers the native MSVC linker), without changing xwin/WSL selection, and test the effective linker environment/config as well as invocation selection.
